<%# The provider's own allowance, behind a button of its own. It used to live at
    the bottom of the report sheet, under a "Kuota" heading three rows down —
    the one reading a reader checks most often was the one they had to scroll
    past the token breakdown to reach.

    It is a `<details>` rather than a dialog so it needs no script to open. The
    panel hangs above the status row instead of pushing it: the row is at the
    bottom edge of the screen, and a panel below it would open off the page.

    The meters are not drawn with the page. They belong to the account, not to
    the session, and only the provider knows them — so they cost a request, and
    the request waits until the reader actually opens this. -%>
<details class="usage-sheet usage-sheet-quota"
         hx-get="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/quota<%= h(token_query) %>"
         hx-target="#usage-quota"
         hx-swap="innerHTML"
         hx-trigger="toggle[this.open]">
  <summary class="usage-toggle" title="Kuota" aria-label="Kuota">
    <%= usage_icon(:quota) %>
  </summary>

  <div class="usage-panel" role="group" aria-label="Kuota">
    <div id="usage-quota" class="usage-quota">
      <p class="usage-note">Memeriksa kuota…</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
